  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "P.Vivekanandan vs The Food Safety Officer on 18 March, 2024 Author: M.Dhandapani Bench: M.Dhandapani Crl.O.P.(MD)No.14628 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 18.03.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice M.Dhandapani Crl.O.P.(MD) No.14628 of 2022 and Crl.M.P.(MD).Nos.9489 and 9492 of 2022 P.Vivekanandan ... Petitioner Vs. The Food Safety Officer, Code No.109 and 120, Chellampatti & Vadipatti Taluk, Designated Officers Office, Multipurpose Health Supervisors (F) Training School, Viswanathapuram, Madurai-625 014. ... Respondent Prayer: Criminal Original Petition is filed under Section 482 of Cr.P.C, to call for the records and quash the proceedings in S.T.C. of 2022 on the file of the Judicial Magistrate, Vadipatti in so far petitioner. For petitioner : Mr.M.Rajaraman For Respondent : Mr.P.Kottaichamy Government Advocate (Crl.Side https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 1/7 Crl.O.P.(MD)N P.Vivekanandan vs The Food Safety Officer on 18 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/132577402/ 1",
    "facts": "A2 and A3 are doing the business of groundnut oil and A3 is the owner of the A2's company. After manufacuturing the groundnut oil, they sent the same for sale through the petitioner. While so, on 25.08.2020, the respondent/food safety officer visited the petitioners factory and taken the sample and sent the same for analysis and the report was received on 19.10.2020. Thereafter, the present complaint was registered on the ground that the edigible oil, which was taken by the food safety officer is unsafe. However, the edigible oil was packed by the manufacuter on 06.03.2020 and it is usable on or before six months (i.e) on 05.09.2020. The analysis was done after the expiry period date, on that sole ground, the prosecution initiated against the co-accused namely A2 and A3 was [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court. 4. The learned Additional Public Prosecutor appearing for the respondent submitted that the food sample was anaylized after the expiry period, on that sole ground, this Court [LEAKAGE_MASK] the complaint in respect of the A2 and A3.",
    "arguments": "The learned conunsel for the petitioner submitted that the petitioner is the retailer and he was arrayed as A1 in the compliant. 6.The learned Counsel appearing for the petitioner during the course of the argument submitted that the period mentioned in the label 'best before' is a mandatory one and he was prevented from selling the https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl.O.P.(MD)No.14628 of 2022 food."
  },
